## Repo map

```
app/            Expo Router routes — THIN (re-export a feature screen, no logic)
src/ui/         Design-system primitives (button, text, text-input) + theme/
src/features/   One folder per feature: screens/ components/ hooks/ api/ types
src/api/        Cross-feature data layer: clients/ (requests) + queries/ (React Query)
src/utilities/  Shared pure helpers (dates, formatters, …)
src/providers/  App-level context providers (mounted in app/_layout.tsx)
src/constants/  env.ts (hand-validated), enums
src/types/      Cross-cutting types
assets/         Images, icons, fonts
```

Each `src/*` folder has its own `README.md` listing what lives there — read it
before adding files, and add a line when you add something notable.

## Core rules (non-negotiable)

- **No barrel files.** Never create an `index.ts(x)` whose only job is
  re-exporting. Import the concrete file (`import { Button } from '@/ui/button'`)
  so every symbol stays traceable to exactly one file.
- **Filename ↔ content.** Kebab-case filenames named after the primary export
  (`shift-card.tsx` → `ShiftCard`, `use-shifts.ts` → `useShifts`). One primary
  export per file; one responsibility per file.
- **Size ceiling: 300 code lines per file** (blanks/comments excluded; tests
  exempt). If a design needs a bigger file, split the design.
- **Tests colocate + use real data.** Sibling `__tests__/`
  (`button.tsx` → `__tests__/button.test.tsx`). Exercise real inputs and real
  integration paths — a test that only proves a mock returns what it was told to
  return is banned.
- **Doc line required.** Every module and public symbol carries a concise doc
  line (leading `/** … */` or `//`). Brief, not optional.
- **Docs in sync.** A change to any user-facing surface (behavior, public API,
  config, scripts) updates the prose that describes it — README, the folder's
  `README.md`, this file — in the same change.
- **No `any`.** No `as any`, `: any`, `as unknown as T`. Use `unknown` + type
  guards.
- **No `console.log` / `debugger`** in committed code. Use `console.warn` /
  `console.error`.

## Gate

`bun run check` runs the full gate and must be green before advancing — even for
an unrelated failure:

```bash
bun run check        # tsc --noEmit + oxlint --deny-warnings + oxfmt --check + check:structure + jest
```

Individual pieces: `bun run type-check`, `bun run lint` (`lint:fix` to auto-fix),
`bun run fmt` / `fmt:check`, `bun run check:structure`, `bun run test`. Pre-commit
(Lefthook) runs oxlint + oxfmt on staged files only. Run tests non-interactively
(`--watchAll=false`).

The structure rules are **enforced, not doc-only**: oxlint (`no-restricted-imports`
for barrel/deep-relative/feature-isolation, `unicorn/filename-case`, `max-lines`)
plus `scripts/check-structure.sh` (allowed `src/` dirs, per-folder READMEs, no
barrel files, `lefthook.yml`). A violation fails the gate.

## Tooling

- Use `bun` for everything (`bun install`, `bun run <script>`, `bunx <bin>`).
- Use `bunx expo install <pkg>` for RN-native deps (SDK-compatible versions),
  `bun add` for pure-JS deps.

## Blocked patterns (pre-commit + CI reject these)

- `as any`, `: any`, `as unknown as T` → use `unknown` + type guards.
- `console.log`, `debugger` → use `console.warn` / `console.error`.
- **Barrel files** (an `index.ts` that only re-exports) → import the concrete
  file. **Sanctioned exception:** `app/**` route files re-export a feature screen
  as a default export (Expo Router requires it) — that is the only place a
  re-export + default export is allowed.
- Tests outside a sibling `__tests__/`; mock-data-only tests.
- Files over 300 lines (tests exempt) → split.

## Conventions

- **Path aliases**: `@/ui/*`, `@/features/*`, `@/api/*`, `@/utilities/*`,
  `@/providers/*`, `@/constants/*`, `@/types/*`, `@/assets/*`. Never deep relative
  imports.
- **Default exports** only in `app/**` (Expo Router needs them); named exports
  everywhere else.
- **Routes are thin**: `app/.../x.tsx` imports a feature screen and re-exports it.
- **Styling**: `StyleSheet.create` + the `src/ui/theme/*` tokens. No styling
  library (no unistyles/nativewind). No hardcoded hex / magic numbers — use theme
  tokens; no inline style object literals for static styles.
- **Data**: server state → React Query (`src/api`); client state → local state /
  React Context (no store library — for genuinely-global client state use
  `createContext` + `useReducer` in `src/providers/`). Never duplicate server data
  into client state.
- **Validation**: env + external/parsed data are validated by hand (type guards
  on `unknown`) — no schema library app-wide. `zod` is allowed **only** inside a
  form (`react-hook-form` + `zodResolver`), with the schema scoped to that form.
- **Commits**: `type(scope): description` (conventional). Push to feature
  branches; never directly to main.

## Style baseline (UI defaults)

Default UI manners for every screen/primitive. Deviate only when the design says
so, and leave a comment when you do.

- **Hide scroll indicators.** Every `ScrollView` / `FlatList` / `SectionList`
  sets `showsVerticalScrollIndicator={false}` and
  `showsHorizontalScrollIndicator={false}`. A visible scrollbar is opt-in.
- **Compose the primitives** (`@/ui/text`, `@/ui/button`, `@/ui/text-input`)
  rather than raw `<Text>` / `<Pressable>` / `<TextInput>`.
- **Respect safe areas** via `react-native-safe-area-context` — never hardcode
  status-bar / notch padding.
- **Touchable + accessible**: interactive elements ≥ 44×44pt with an
  `accessibilityRole` + label.
- **Right list for the job**: virtualized `FlatList`/`SectionList` for long
  lists; `ScrollView` only for short, finite content. Use
  `keyboardShouldPersistTaps="handled"` when a scroll view holds inputs.

